Overall Water Splitting Performances of the Series of $\mathbf{Co_{x}N i_{3-x}(H A B)_{2}}$ MOF Catalysts. Given that the constructed $\mathrm{Co_{x}N i_{3-x}(H A B)_{2}}$ MOF-2 catalyst displays excellent HER and OER performances, it can be a promising electrochemical catalyst for overall water electrolysis. A two-electrode water electrolysis device with $\mathrm{Co}_{\mathrm{x}}\mathrm{Ni}_{3}$ - $\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\mathrm{x}}(\mathrm{HAB})_{2}$ MOF-2 as the anode and cathode was packaged and utilized in 1.0 M KOH solution. Meanwhile, other MOFs were used as electrocatalysts for overall water splitting for comparison. As illustrated in Fig. 6a, the current density at the cell voltage of $1.45\mathrm{V}$ of $\mathrm{Co_{x}N i_{3-x}(H A B)_{2}M O F{-}{2}}$ is $10\mathrm{mAcm}^{-2}$ , lower than those of the $\mathrm{Co}_{3}(\mathrm{HAB})_{2}$ MOF (1.48 V), $\mathrm{Ni}_{3}(\mathrm{HAB})_{2}$ MOF (1.46 V), $\mathrm{Co_{x}N i_{3-x}(H A B)_{2}}$ MOF-1 (1.52 V), $\mathrm{Co}_{\mathrm{x}}\mathrm{Ni}_{3}.$ - $\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\mathrm{x}}(\mathrm{HAB})_{2}$ MOF-3 (1.47 V), and Pt/C ∥ ${\mathrm{RuO}}_{2}$ (1.59 V) catalysts (Table S10). The overpotential for driving the current density of $10\mathrm{mA}\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ of $\mathrm{Co_{x}N i_{3-x}(H A B)_{2}}$ MOF2 is substantially smaller than those of the reported Co-, Ni-, or MOF-based catalysts (Fig. 6d and Table S12). Concurrently, LSV curves were recorded in a three-electrode system with the potential range of $-1.2–1.6\mathrm{~V~}_{1}$ s. RHE. The voltage gap $(\Delta E)$ required to yield $10\mathrm{\mA\cm}^{-2}$ for HER and OER ( $\Delta E=E_{\mathrm{OER}}$ , $\scriptstyle\mathrm{j=10}-E_{\mathrm{HER,~j=10}})$ is a significant parameter in evaluating catalytic activities for overall water splitting. A small $\Delta E$ value represents outstanding overall water splitting performance [73]. Fig. 6b shows that the $\Delta E$ of $\mathrm{Co_{x}N i_{3-x}(H A B)_{2}}$ MOF-2 is as low as $1.52\mathrm{V}$ , lower than those of the $\mathrm{Co}_{3}(\mathrm{HAB})_{2}$ MOF $(1.63{\mathrm{~V}})$ , the $\mathrm{Ni}_{3}(\mathrm{HAB})_{2}$ MOF (1.58 V), $\mathrm{Co_{x}N i_{3-x}(H A B)_{2}}$ MOF-1 (1.56 V), and $\mathrm{Co_{x}N i_{3-x}(H A B)_{2}}$ MOF-3 (1.59 V) (Table S11). Notably, the $\Delta E$ value of $\mathrm{Co}_{\mathrm{x}}\mathrm{Ni}_{3}$ - $_\mathrm{x}(\mathrm{HAB})_{2}\mathrm{MOF}{-2}$ is lower than that of other reported catalysts, such as CF–NG–Co (1.69
